/target
Cargo.lock.bak
.idea/
.claude/

# `cargo mutants` writes here when nothing passes `--output`, and a run
# leaves tens of thousands of files across its `log/` and `diff/` trees.
# Untracked is not enough on its own: `release-plz` refuses to compute a
# version while the working directory is dirty, so a forgotten `--output`
# blocks a release until somebody notices what the directory is.
#
# **`.old` is the tool's own doing and the rule was one run short of it.**
# `cargo mutants` renames the previous `mutants.out/` to `mutants.out.old/`
# before it starts, so the second sweep in a row leaves a directory this
# rule did not name — 3.2 MB of it, untracked, producing exactly the
# release failure the paragraph above describes. Found by running two
# sweeps rather than by reading the rule.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Playwright/MCP scratch, from browser measurements
.playwright-mcp/
/.spike-target

# Spikes: throwaway crates that prove a shape before it is built.
# Their findings live in docs/; the code itself is not carried, because
# nothing builds it and an unbuilt crate rots into a lie.
spikes/

# The project's own memory: design notes, acceptance records, research and
# measurements kept from building it. Untracked on purpose — it is written
# for whoever works on this, not for whoever uses it, and `docs/` is for
# the second audience. Everything here was in git until it was moved, so
# the history still holds it; what is not wanted is a published crate
# shipping a reader an archive of how it came to be.
.notes/
